h \\n. Also need to escape any occurrence of backslash, but there are none. Also, we need to escape the double quotes that will enclose the code string in JSON. Since we used single quotes in code, no double quotes to escape.\n\nHowever, the code has indentation using spaces. That's fine.\n\nNow produce the final JSON.\n\nWe must ensure that the first non-whitespace character is { and last is }. So the JSON object must start with { and end with }.\n\nLet's produce:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    if not segments:\\n        raise ValueError('No segments')\\n    order = []\\n    for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\\n        if not all(k in seg for k in ('name','importance','minimum','capacity')):\\n            raise ValueError(f'Segment {i} missing field')\\n        order.append(seg['name'])\\n    sum_min = sum(s['minimum'] for s in segments)\\n    sum_cap = sum(s['capacity'] for s in segments)\\n    if budget < sum_min or budget > sum_cap:\\n        raise ValueError(f'Budget {budget} out of range [{sum_min}, {sum_cap}]')\\n    alloc = {s['name']: s['minimum'] for s in segments}\\n    remaining = budget - sum_min\\n    caps = {s['name']: s['capacity'] for s in segments}\\n    imps = {s['name']: s['importance'] for s in segments}\\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        best_priority = -1.0\\n        for i, name in enumerate(order):\\n            if alloc[name] < caps[name]:\\n                priority = imps[name] / (alloc[name] + 1.0)\\n                if priority > best_priority:\\n                    best_priority = priority\\n                    best_idx = i\\n        if best_idx == -1:\\n            break\\n        best_name = order[best_idx]\\n        alloc[best_name] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    total = sum(alloc.values())\\n    return {'allocations': alloc, 'name_mapping': order, 'total': total}\"}\n\nBut we need to ensure the code is properly indented and